BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTSTAMP:20261003T145204Z
UID:a11cb847b167f6db3762e7d7aba4@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular: The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, presente
 d by Citizens\, returns October 1 &#8211\; November 1 with an all-new trai
 l of clever carvings guaranteed to make you smile\, groan\, and laugh out 
 loud. This year’s theme celebrates the art of the pun\, with thousands o
 f hand-carved pumpkins bringing witty wordplay to life through pop culture
  references\, playful characters and pun-believable scenes. From clever on
 e-liners to delightfully cheesy dad jokes\, there’s something to make ev
 ery guest grin as they stroll The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, where over 5\,000 
 glowing jack-o’-lanterns illuminate the Zoo. Don’t miss New England’
 s “must-see” family-friendly event of the Halloween season at Roger Wi
 lliams Park Zoo. All tickets must be purchased online in advance. Tickets 
 are required and sold online only. No refunds or rescheduling. Buy Tickets
 \n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacu
 lar/92071/
LOCATION:Roger Williams Park Zoo\, 1000 Elmwood Avenue\, Providence\, RI 0
 2907
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacular/9207
 1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Skyward:" Anne Patterson & James Teschner
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTSTAMP:20261003T145204Z
UID:dd258d572b2bb46d7f0627f62f8e@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:"Skyward:" Anne Patterson &amp\; James Teschner Exhibition Dat
 es: September 5- October 3\, 2026 Opening Reception: Saturday September 5
 \, 2026\, 5:00- 7:00 PM "Skyward:" Anne Patterson &amp\; James Teschner Je
 ssica Hagen Fine Art + Design is pleased to announce the opening of "Skywa
 rd" featuring artists James Teschner and Anne Patterson on Saturday Septem
 ber 5\, 2026\, from 5:00- 7:00 PM. This exhibition showcases the paintings
  of James Teschner and the sculptural orbs of Anne Patterson. Teschner\, p
 ainting outdoors near his home in the remote farmlands of central France f
 ocuses on the setting sun\, the moon\, the sky\, and “those moments lead
 ing towards nightfall\, and the night itself\, whereby the landscape is ei
 ther being obliterated\, almost devoured by the sun’s all-consuming lumi
 nosity or being dissolved by the receding\, diminishing light.” Anne Pat
 terson is a multi-disciplinary artist based in Brooklyn. Working across pa
 inting\, sculpture\, and installation\, Patterson explores the ways our se
 nses overlap\, and how together they create an experience greater than the
  sum of its parts. Informed by her own synesthesia and her training as a s
 et designer\, she is often inspired by music and sound. Gallery owner Jess
 ica Hagen states\, “This is a magical exhibition. The radiance of James 
 Teschner’s oil paintings coalesce with the glow of Anne Patterson’s go
 ld-leafed orbs\, resulting in a sublime alchemy. It’s really a very spec
 ial show.” "Skyward" closes October 3\, 2026. Jessica Hagen Fine Art + D
 esign was founded in 2005 and features contemporary art including painting
 \, sculpture\, photography\, ceramics\, textiles\, and jewelry. Located in
  the historic Point section of Newport\, the gallery’s hours are Wednesd
 ay- Saturday 11:00 AM - 5:00 PM and Sunday 12:00- 5:00 PM. The gallery is 
 also open by appointment.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/even
 t/skyward%3a-anne-patterson-%26-james-teschner/111508/
LOCATION:Jessica Hagen Fine Art & Design\, 9A Bridge Street\, Newport\, RI
  02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/skyward%3a-anne-patterson-%26-j
 ames-teschner/111508/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A New England Thanksgiving
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTSTAMP:20261003T145204Z
UID:6a190c212ccbb51c1f1bb6e80fbb@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join the Coggeshall staff as we prepare a Thanksgiving meal ov
 er the hearth in our historic farmhouse. The late 18th century was before 
 the official start of Thanksgiving as a national holiday\, but the day was
  still celebrated with food and prayer in New England. Watch our costumed 
 historians make chicken on a string\, bake a pie in the hot coals\, mash t
 urnips and churn butter. In the woodshop we will also demonstrate carving 
 wooden spoons. Explore the garden to see the last of the fall harvest. Wal
 k the nature trail and look for signs of wild turkey\, see musket demonstr
 ations and try your aim with rubber band targets. Please note: This is not
  a Thanksgiving meal for visitors to eat. Food prepared in the historic Fa
 rmhouse Kitchen does not meet modern health and food preparation codes for
  public consumption.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-n
 ew-england-thanksgiving/112116/
LOCATION:Coggeshall Farm Museum\, 1 Colt Drive\, Bristol\, 02809 Time: 10:
 00 AM to 4:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-new-england-thanksgiving/1121
 16/
END:VEVENT
